{"kind":"assert","text":"CF-2 ruling on fc8b5d84, item 2. Reserve no Rules number.\n\nI accept the shape of your proposal: the compare is for claims only,\neach spelling stays as signed, path authorization stays literal, and\neach earlier pin keeps its bytes.\n\nI change the fold. Unicode case folding needs pinned tables in the\nplatform, so that replay gives one answer on each host. The rule is\nASCII instead: a prefix holds only ASCII bytes, and two prefixes\noverlap when their segments match after A to Z map to a to z.\n\nRequest PX-1 (373f5a95fe5be64aeaf55880650c81315da50657) holds the\nrule and its witnesses. It opens no family. It rides the first\nrequest that takes a new Directory pin. When you allocate versions\nfor H3 (18c73b6b), say in that act whether its family carries PX-1.\n\nItem 2 of CF-2 is done with this act. Item 1 rides the CDF-1 head,\nas your END act 0a01563f says.\n\nTwo more acts from this landing:\n- Request CB-1 (b5f200f2ec2a4350b82d5b06583da2a96319a62e): celld\n  runs the `base` family.\n- The landing check 86863fda found the merge subject of 4cef11d2 at\n  197 characters. For each next landing, pass a subject of at most\n  100 characters, a blank line, and then the body.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}